    "created_at": "2026-01-20T18:57:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-20T18:57:38Z",
    "body": "I'd like to revive this issue. @domenic was right that implementations do not currently type-check the chunks enqueued on streams. However, one of the largest uses of `ReadableStream` in particular are the streams created by the browser and consumed by script. It would improve ergonomics for TypeScript developers for WebIDL to define the chunk type for such streams. As mentioned, comments are not normative and since people are writing automatic converters from WebIDL to TypeScript type definitions it would be helpful for chunk types to be normatively specified somewhere other than only the algorithms.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
